{"text": "2 PIC S9(9).\n\n\n       PROCEDURE DIVISION.\n\n\n       ENTRY-PARA.\n           PERFORM MAIN-PARA\n           STOP RUN.\n\n\n       MAIN-PARA.\n      * Display 8 per line\n      * Count the number of prime numbers\n       MOVE 0 TO count_main\n       DISPLAY \"The prime numbers between 2 and 1,000, inclusive are \\n\"\n      * Repeatedly find prime numbers\n       PERFORM VARYING number_main FROM 2 BY 1 UNTIL NOT (number_main <= 1000)\n      * Assume the number is prime\n      * Is the current number prime?\n       MOVE 'Y' TO isPrime_main\n      * Test whether number is prime\n       COMPUTE TEMP_0 = number_main / 2\n       PERFORM VARYING divisor_main FROM 2 BY 1 UNTIL NOT (divisor_main <= TEMP_0)\n       DIVIDE number_main BY divisor_main GIVING TEMP_1 REMAINDER TEMP_1\n       IF TEMP_1 = 0\n      * If true, number is not prime\n      * Set isPrime to false\n       MOVE 'N' TO isPrime_main\n      * Exit the for loop\n"}
{"text": "<|fim_prefix|> PROCEDURE DIVISION.\n\n\n       ENTRY-PARA.\n           PERFORM MAIN-PARA\n           STOP RUN.\n\n\n       MAIN-PARA.\n      * Display 8 per line\n      * Count the number of prime numbers\n       MOVE 0 TO count_main\n       DISPLAY \"The prime numbers between 2 and 1,000, inclusive are \\n\"\n      * Repeatedly find prime numbers\n       PERFORM VARYING number_main FROM 2 BY 1 UNTIL NOT<|fim_suffix|> REMAINDER TEMP_1\n       IF TEMP_1 = 0\n      * If true, number is not prime\n      * Set isPrime to false\n       MOVE 'N' TO isPrime_main\n      * Exit the for loop\n       EXIT PERFORM\n       END-<|fim_middle|> (number_main <= 1000)\n      * Assume the number is prime\n      * Is the current number prime?\n       MOVE 'Y' TO isPrime_main\n      * Test whether number is prime\n       COMPUTE TEMP_0 = number_main / 2\n       PERFORM VARYING divisor_main FROM 2 BY 1 UNTIL NOT (divisor_main <= TEMP_0)\n       DIVIDE number_main BY divisor_main GIVING"}
{"text": "ARA.\n           PERFORM MAIN-PARA\n           STOP RUN.\n\n\n       MAIN-PARA.\n      * Display 8 per line\n      * Count the number of prime numbers\n       MOVE 0 TO count_main\n       DISPLAY \"The prime numbers between 2 and 1,000, inclusive are \\n\"\n      * Repeatedly find prime numbers\n       PERFORM VARYING number_main FROM 2 BY 1 UNTIL NOT (number_main <= 1000)\n      * Assume the number is prime\n      * Is the current number prime?\n       MOVE 'Y' TO isPrime_main\n      * Test whether number is prime\n       COMPUTE TEMP_0 = number_main / 2\n       PERFORM VARYING divisor_main FROM 2 BY 1 UNTIL NOT (divisor_main <= TEMP_0)\n       DIVIDE number_main BY divisor_main GIVING TEMP_1 REMAINDER TEMP_1\n       IF TEMP_1 = 0\n      * If true, number is not prime\n      * Set isPrime to false\n       MOVE 'N' TO isPrime_main\n      * Exit the for loop\n       EXIT PERFORM\n       END-IF\n       COMPUTE TEMP_0"}
{"text": "\n           STOP RUN.\n\n\n       MAIN-PARA.\n      * Display 8 per line\n      * Count the number of prime numbers\n       MOVE 0 TO count_main\n       DISPLAY \"The prime numbers between 2 and 1,000, inclusive are \\n\"\n      * Repeatedly find prime numbers\n       PERFORM VARYING number_main FROM 2 BY 1 UNTIL NOT (number_main <= 1000)\n      * Assume the number is prime\n      * Is the current number prime?\n       MOVE 'Y' TO isPrime_main\n      * Test whether number is prime\n       COMPUTE TEMP_0 = number_main / 2\n       PERFORM VARYING divisor_main FROM 2 BY 1 UNTIL NOT (divisor_main <= TEMP_0)\n       DIVIDE number_main BY divisor_main GIVING TEMP_1 REMAINDER TEMP_1\n       IF TEMP_1 = 0\n      * If true, number is not prime\n      * Set isPrime to false\n       MOVE 'N' TO isPrime_main\n      * Exit the for loop\n       EXIT PERFORM\n       END-IF\n       COMPUTE TEMP_0 = number_main / 2\n      "}
